> hearse: uploading bones
> hearse: bonD0.6 offering to server
> bzip2: Can't open input file /var/games/nethack/bonD0.6.bz2: Permission
> denied.
> hearse: error reading bzip2 -dc \/var\/games\/nethack\/bonD0\.6\.bz2|: exit
> status 256
> --
>
> The bones files are owned by the user whose game created them ('jon'), and
> belong to the group 'users'.

hearse drops root privileges and runs as games:games by default, so
it can't read your jon:users bones files unless they are readable for
everybody.

The best solution IMO would be to make NetHack sgid games if your
distribution doesn't prevent that so the bones files would belong to
jon:games and be readable for hearse. Otherwise, if you can make sure
that all NetHack players are in group "users" running hearse with the
run-as-group option should help. In any case check your bones-mode
option.

For more information:

less /usr/games/bin/hearse
man hearse

> Changing ownership to 'games:games' and running hearse again gets this:
> --
> hearse: no bones to upload

You already offered that file to the hearse server. Probably it won't
be accepted a second time despite the fact that it wasn't actually
uploaded. Try a new bones file.


